 "_doc": "Wall colour samples of the area kits (P2-010 fix round, decisions.md 2026-11-14 'Areas are built from how they look today'). For every kit: its area board (harness/design/areas/<board>_board.jpg) and rectangles [x, y, w, h] in board pixels, each on a plain wall of one photo (`photo` is the number printed on the board). tools/kits/sample_walls.mjs reads the median wall colour of each rectangle (darkest fifth and brightest tenth dropped: shadow and glare), writes the kit's `walls` (samples with their photo, the colours, the hue, saturation and value range, the palette word map) into game/world/kits/kits.json, and a crop sheet to harness/reports/kits/wall_samples.jpg to check each rectangle sits on a wall. Bright colour on goods, signs and awnings is not sampled: walls only. `cap` is the brightest channel a wall colour may have (sRGB 0 to 255; a kit may set its own): the afternoon sun clips a lit wall brighter than about 190 to flat white (measured on kit_colonnade and kit_railings_close), so the CP whitewash takes 168 and its columns and arches keep their shading. `lift`: when a board's photos are dull (haze, shade), the kit's colours are lifted together until the brightest reaches this value (0 to 1).",
